<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div>
    <div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;">
      <details class="sc-faq" open>
      <summary>Which processes does Hana run robotically?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Hana uses robotic and automated systems for soldering, selective and laser soldering, conformal coating, potting, chemical de-burr, singulation and package pack-out.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Can singulation run without an operator?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. Auto-singulation can run operator-free, using e-map data to identify and automatically scrap defective units.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>How is high-volume test automated?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Turret, gravity and tray-to-tray handlers can feed automated test equipment, with film-frame handling and map-driven sorting available for die-level processes.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>Does Hana provide in-line PCB and package inspection?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">Yes. SMT inspection capabilities include 3D SPI, pre- and post-reflow AOI and X-ray. At package level, Hana also provides automated fillet-height inspection and six-sided optical AOI with automatic offload.</div>
    </details>
      <details class="sc-faq">
      <summary>What inspection resolution is available, and can hidden joints be verified?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary>
      <div class="sc-faq-a">3D AOI is available to 7 &micro;m resolution, with SPI camera resolution of 20 &micro;m in x/y. 2D and 3D X-ray can inspect features including voids, wire pitch and ball pitch where optical inspection does not provide direct visibility.</div>
    </details>
